<!--
  RM_GlassChain_Items.xml                 RimMandrake — STILLSAND_GLASS_LENS_CHAIN_1 §1-4

  Sand to glass to lens. Owner, typed (volley turn 2): "the very fine sand of this region is
  extremely high quality and can be smelted into a fine glass fit for lenses."

    RM_GlassSand    shovelled drift. Every drift is stock (MovingDunes' clear-yield, bound to
                    RM_Stillsand in MovingDunes/Patches/BiomeBindings.xml).
    RM_FineSand     the owner's "simply Fine Sand": a trade commodity; one of its uses is
                    lens-grade glass. The sieve that makes it from glass sand is NOT built yet
                    (feasibility reported on the item; owner picks chore vs Sand Sieve).
    RM_SunGlass     plain glass from the sun furnace. One stuff, one stat line, one market
                    value, provisional until DESIGN_MATERIALS_REVIEW_1.
    RM_LensGlass    lens-grade glass from fine sand. Art: reuses the sun-glass icon, tinted
                    (no job of its own).
    RM_PrecisionLens / RM_PearlLens   ground at the lens bench. The krayt lens is RSW tier
                    (an RSW patch recipe), not built here.

  Art: artpipe jobs RM_GlassSand, RM_LensSand (delivers the fine-sand icon; filed before the
  rename), RM_SunGlass, RM_PrecisionLens, RM_PearlLens. Each texPath is where that art lands.
-->
<Defs>

  <ThingDef ParentName="ResourceBase">
    <defName>RM_GlassSand</defName>
    <label>glass sand</label>
    <description>Pale, clean drift sand shovelled off a dune field. The grains are almost pure silica, worn round by the wind, with very little clay or iron in them. A sun furnace melts it into plain glass, and a sieve can pull the finest grains out of it.</description>
    <graphicData>
      <!-- art pending: artpipe RM_GlassSand -->
      <texPath>Things/Item/Resource/RM_GlassSand</texPath>
      <graphicClass>Graphic_Single</graphicClass>
    </graphicData>
    <soundInteract>Standard_Drop</soundInteract>
    <soundDrop>Standard_Drop</soundDrop>
    <stackLimit>75</stackLimit>
    <useHitPoints>false</useHitPoints>
    <healthAffectsPrice>false</healthAffectsPrice>
    <statBases>
      <MarketValue>0.3</MarketValue>
      <Mass>0.5</Mass>
      <Flammability>0</Flammability>
      <DeteriorationRate>0</DeteriorationRate>
    </statBases>
    <thingCategories>
      <li>ResourcesRaw</li>
    </thingCategories>
    <techLevel>Neolithic</techLevel>
  </ThingDef>

  <ThingDef ParentName="ResourceBase">
    <defName>RM_FineSand</defName>
    <label>fine sand</label>
    <description>The finest grains of desert silica, sifted clean and graded small. Traders buy it by the sack: glassmakers want it for high-quality glass, and it has other uses besides. A sun furnace melts it into lens glass.</description>
    <graphicData>
      <!-- art pending: artpipe RM_LensSand (filed under the old name) -->
      <texPath>Things/Item/Resource/RM_FineSand</texPath>
      <graphicClass>Graphic_Single</graphicClass>
    </graphicData>
    <soundInteract>Standard_Drop</soundInteract>
    <soundDrop>Standard_Drop</soundDrop>
    <stackLimit>75</stackLimit>
    <useHitPoints>false</useHitPoints>
    <healthAffectsPrice>false</healthAffectsPrice>
    <statBases>
      <MarketValue>2.2</MarketValue>
      <Mass>0.4</Mass>
      <Flammability>0</Flammability>
      <DeteriorationRate>0</DeteriorationRate>
    </statBases>
    <thingCategories>
      <li>ResourcesRaw</li>
    </thingCategories>
    <tradeability>All</tradeability>
    <tradeTags>
      <li>ExoticMisc</li>
    </tradeTags>
    <techLevel>Neolithic</techLevel>
  </ThingDef>

  <ThingDef ParentName="ResourceBase">
    <defName>RM_SunGlass</defName>
    <label>sun glass</label>
    <description>Thick, clear glass with a faint gold tint, melted out of desert sand by focused sunlight. It is good for glazing, still lids and ornament, and it builds well. It is not clear enough to grind into a lens.</description>
